An integer is numerically balanced if every digit $d$ present in the number appears exactly $d$ times (meaning $0$ cannot appear). 

Given that $n \le 10^6$, the smallest numerically balanced number strictly greater than $666666$ is $1224444$ (the smallest 7-digit balanced number, formed by digits `1`, `2`, `2`, `4`, `4`, `4`, `4`). Any $n$ in the range $[666666, 10^6]$ will therefore directly have $1224444$ as the answer. For $n < 666666$, the gap to the next balanced number is small enough that we can check numbers sequentially starting from $n + 1$.

Here is the complete solution:

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param Integer $n
     * @return Integer
     */
    function nextBeautifulNumber($n) {
        if ($n >= 666666) {
            return 1224444;
        }

        for ($i = $n + 1; ; $i++) {
            if ($this->isBalanced($i)) {
                return $i;
            }
        }
    }

    private function isBalanced($x) {
        $count = array_fill(0, 10, 0);
        $temp = $x;

        while ($temp > 0) {
            $d = $temp % 10;
            if ($d === 0) {
                return false;
            }
            $count[$d]++;
            $temp = intdiv($temp, 10);
        }

        for ($d = 1; $d <= 7; $d++) {
            if ($count[$d] !== 0 && $count[$d] !== $d) {
                return false;
            }
        }

        return true;
    }
}
